  "qualityNotes": [
    "Five capital populated places, GeoNames P/PPLC: Astana 1526273, Tashkent 1512569, Bishkek 1528675, Dushanbe 1221874, Ashgabat 162183; all distinct from ADM1 and airports.",
    "Astana renaming chronology: 1961-03-20 Akmolinsk→Tselinograd; 1992-07-06 Tselinograd→Aqmola; 1998-05-06 Aqmola→Astana; 2019-03-23 Astana→Nur-Sultan; 2022 return to Astana.",
    "Astana's 2022-09-17 decree signature and 2022-09-19 official published act are different dates. This staging explicitly selects 2022-09-19 for legal-effective Korean map label; do not silently equate signing/publication.",
    "Bishkek renaming dates 1926-05-12 Pishpek→Frunze and 1991-02-05 Frunze→Bishkek are supported by Kyrgyz city hall and a parliamentary act. An older city-hall English overview mentions April 1991 and is kept as a source discrepancy.",
    "Dushanbe 1929 Stalinabad renaming and 1961 restoration use year precision, because the contemporary renaming and central approval dates in 1929 are not identical in secondary accounts.",
    "Ashgabat was renamed Poltoratsk in 1919 and restored 1927-04-07; native Türkmen Aşgabat and Russian Ашхабад differ by language. A switch to modern Korean 아시가바트 from Turkmen independence in 1991 is explicitly an editorial transcription policy, not a legal city renaming.",
    "Tashkent's Uzbek Toshkent, Cyrillic Тошкент and Russian Ташкент forms coexist; the 1930 capital transfer from Samarkand is not an official city-name change.",
    "Akmola fort 1830, modern Pishpek settlement 1868, and modern Askhabad administrative town 1881 are temporal city eligibility rules; earlier settlements or ruins at the sites are not automatically equated to each modern city ID.",
    "SourceCountryCode is modern GeoNames metadata only, never sufficient for sovereign assignment of historical periods. UI short name notes/details <=28 Unicode codepoints; researchDetail and researchNote preserve complex sourcing.",
    "Review staging only; no live PLAC v2 tile, map manifest or main branch changed."
